+# GS-017 playthrough usability and patient flow
+
+## Goal and authorization
+Implement owner-approved GS-011-006 (alert overload), GS-011-008 (one-action chart close after wrong answer), and diagnose/fix GS-011-009 (day-six patient shortage), sequentially. Owner acceptance is pending; no renewed batch approval is required.
+
+## Constraints and starting state
+Repository is on beta, starting HEAD c26c96a111103d8665e33c9258ef54071d729f14, with extensive inherited dirty work. Starting diff, status, HEAD, and copies of changed/untracked files are in ignored `.local-dev/gs-017-baseline/`. Compare against those copies, not HEAD alone. Preserve GS-016's accepted tutorial construction, room requirements and saves; GS-015 room design and GS-013 renderer/art are excluded. Clinical content belongs to GS-006. No new clinical content, altered approval gates, schedule resets, economy changes, owner-save access, live-server restart, publication or PM-board edits.
+
+## Ownership and decisions
+Astra owns this plan, `docs/handoffs/GS-017_PLAYTHROUGH_BATCH.md`, integration/review and narrow GS-011-006/008/009 feedback entries. One named write worker at a time; workers do not delegate or commit. Workers must identify exact source/test paths before edits and preserve inherited hunks.
+
+## Milestones and acceptance
+1. Terra: trace alert production and presentation, reduce routine repetitions while preserving active warnings and useful history. Demonstrate concrete before/after counts under representative bursts. Initial allowed investigation: alert view models, MessageBoard UI, alert configuration/domain scheduling. Exact edit ownership recorded before implementation.
+2. Terra: reproduce wrong-answer close sequence, fix actual cause, retain explanation, explicit correct answer after submission, distinct findings, scoring, decisions and re-entry. Focused wrong/correct regressions.
+3. Sol or Terra: diagnose arrivals, eligible content, review scheduling, pending tests, reachability, unlock/filtering. Demonstrate day six and beyond under supported conditions. Fix scoped bug if established; otherwise precisely document eligible exhaustion and content follow-up without claiming resolution.
+4. Delegated combined isolated browser acceptance, including realistic event burst, correct/wrong answer routes and GS-016 fresh campaign construction regression. Parent reviews actual diffs, tests and screenshots.
+
+## Validation
+Focused meaningful Vitest tests after each milestone. Final player/domain suites with bounded concurrency, workspace typechecks, boundaries, isolated player build. Browser uses disposable contexts and a separate loopback server/build, never owner's 4173 session or normal build output. Canonical owner opening remains START_GAME.cmd -> http://127.0.0.1:4173; isolated test storage is separate.
+
+## Progress and next action
+- Read repository instructions, feedback and GS-016 handoff; inspected GS-006 latest clinical totals (143 concepts, 350 cases, 543 nodes) and GS-015 ownership.
+- Captured pre-implementation baseline.
+- Terra `alerts_milestone` owns milestone 1: `apps/player/src/session/alertViewModels.ts` and `alertViewModels.test.ts`; optional scoped `apps/player/src/ui/EventMessageBoard.tsx`, `EventMessageBoard.test.tsx`, `types.ts` for player-accessible grouped history. No domain/config timing change. Parent requires accessible history, not merely retained raw state.
+- Milestone 1 implemented/reviewed: stable routine groups expose dated original history, active warnings remain standalone. Mixed fixture uses four naturally generated ambient events plus three seeded water-condition occurrences: seven to three nonpersistent rows (57%); not a whole-session all-feed measurement. Parent reviewed actual baseline-relative diffs and independently passed 39 focused tests; worker full player 437/437 and player typecheck passed. Boundaries passed independently.
+- Same Terra worker owns milestone 2: session `usePrototypeSession.ts`, `viewModels.ts`, UI `types.ts` and `ChartPanel.tsx`, focused player tests/new close helper if needed. No domain reducer edit. Reproduction confirms terminal Dismiss acknowledges but stays open; header Close leaves unacknowledged feedback. Approved product behavior: deliberate close acknowledges visible pending feedback, stops on rejection, then closes only if still open; terminal primary says Dismiss and close chart. Intermediate Enact Plan remains a continue action; header close preserves required later work. Preserve ADR0026/0030 acknowledgment and future decision gates.
+- Milestone 2 implemented and parent source reviewed: single visible-feedback acknowledgment before close; failed acknowledgment stops closing; naturally closed service route avoids duplicate close. Terminal primary routes to close. New `session/chartCloseBehavior.ts`; modified hook/view model/UI and `chartFeedbackPresentation.test.tsx`. Parent rejected an acknowledgment loop that could consume newly created teaching, worker removed it. Parent independently passed chart/tutorial 8 tests; worker domain game-domain 9 and player typecheck passed. Combined browser still required for real hook clicks.
+- Sol `patient_supply` owns new `packages/game-domain/tests/patient-supply.test.ts` for milestone 3; `clinical-selection.ts` and `reducer.ts` are read-only pending proof of a runtime defect and exact expanded ownership. Need current-library stage/capability eligibility, review-clock/exhaustion limits, and normal-command day 6–8+ evidence without altering policy.
+- Parent integrated M1/M2 check: player 438/438 across 72 files and all workspace typechecks pass.
+- Milestone3 diagnosis completed: normal-tick extended run through 4800 ticks admitted/completed 78 patients with daily arrivals 11/10/9/10/9/10/10/9. At day 8 end, no due reviews/pending work and selector null; two unseen concepts blocked by learned not-due siblings. No runtime fix warranted without changing review policy; exact content follow-up in scoped handoff. Sol reported extended test 54.25s pass; parent independently passed the full domain suite and sustained proof. Sol was interrupted after sufficient diagnostic evidence to prevent further expansion.
+- Terra prepared isolated preview at 4187 and attempted GS-016 browser acceptance, but its opaque runner stalled without usable receipt. Sol `patient_supply` now owns diagnosis/completion of browser acceptance in new `tests/e2e/playthrough-batch.spec.ts` and batch-specific screenshots. No source behavior changes unless parent reviews a demonstrated defect. Use isolated production preview and disposable Chrome; preserve GS-016 screenshots. Parent owns final suite execution and visual/diff review.
+- Parent full domain 325/325 passed. Independent extended diagnostic also passed; discovery listed two copies of the same proof. Parent retained Sol's formatted `packages/game-domain/tests/diagnostics/patient-supply.test.ts`, removed only the new duplicate root copy, and tightened its operation guard to 10,000 (also passed in the duplicate). No runtime change. Canonical extended command: `npm run test --workspace @gamify-surgery/game-domain -- tests/diagnostics/patient-supply.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`.
+- Resume after owner-reported usage reset: reread repository instructions/plan, inspected shared tree and workers. Sol's browser turn had errored on usage; resumed the same named worker and existing `tests/e2e/playthrough-batch.spec.ts`. No reset credit used. Completed checks remain valid.
+- Browser timeout cause established: existing GS-016 spec waits for DEV-only `__facilityGame`, which is intentionally absent in the isolated production build. This was a test-environment mismatch, not app/Chrome failure. Sol's new batch spec exercises production canvas controls and retains original GS-016 screenshots. Parent independently reached the empty test campaign screen via CUA and closed its temporary tabs; no owner session interaction.
+- Final browser acceptance: four production scenarios passed in 1.5 minutes; fresh tutorial/construction/persistence passed in 1.8 minutes on isolated development preview using the exact layout hook. Parent read the receipt, inspected test changes and reviewed all six screenshots. No runtime change was needed for test-coordinate, departure-wait or upkeep-assertion corrections. Production coordinate guesses were removed.
+- Final scoped audit covers 16 source/test/document paths against the captured starting state, plus six batch screenshots. Reducer, selectors, balance settings and facility renderer match the starting snapshot. Concurrent GS-011 intake additions in the shared feedback log are unrelated and excluded from batch ownership. Both temporary preview listeners (4187 and 4188) were verified stopped after review. Owner acceptance remains pending; next action is owner playtest and feedback.
+
+## Closeout
+Record each item's technical status separately from owner acceptance. Present batch for owner playtest. After owner agrees complete, scoped audit/commit/GitHub backup with remote verification and archival are authorized; no merge/deployment. Preserve all unrelated work.
+
+## Owner-requested alert revision (2026-09-17)
+The owner rejected expandable grouping and authorized restoring the plain feed while reducing actual notification volume. This supersedes the original M1 acceptance, including its no-alert-timing-change restriction. Preserve the chart-close fix, patient-supply diagnosis, clinical content, simulation/economy timing, owner campaign and unrelated work. Revision baseline is `.local-dev/gs-017-alert-revision-baseline/`; original pre-GS017 baseline remains available to remove only grouping changes.
+
+Requirements: suppress patient check-in and result-return feed messages; waiting alert after 60 facility minutes; water-empty and litter alerts only after 60 minutes and at most once per facility day (litter globally, no accumulation spam); inner-peace only after 60 minutes without an arrival and once daily; each patient amenity/staff complaint at most daily and staggered; room-upgrade complaints from level 3 only, at most every two days and staggered; ambient humor no more than every 120 facility minutes. Use the configured operating-day length, not wall-clock time. Prefer rolling minimum intervals to avoid day-boundary bursts. Stagger complaint categories by at least 60 facility minutes; do not emit a catch-up burst. Patient waiting should notify once per continuous waiting episode unless later review establishes an existing necessary escalation.
+
+Milestones: Terra investigates exact scheduling/presentation ownership, then implements a bounded alert-only revision with real threshold/cooldown/persistence tests and removes grouping. Astra reviews source diff, acceptance boundaries and migration behavior, then delegates any necessary corrections or isolated browser validation. No new gameplay level is authorized; current level cap means upgrade complaints stay silent until future level-3 support. Preserve genuinely urgent/system feedback.
+
+Status: revision in progress; prior M1 result is superseded. Parent owns plan/handoff and the GS-011-006 feedback entry. Worker owns identified alert source/tests only, reports exact paths before edits, and does not edit durable planning, commit, push, deploy, install dependencies, touch owner server/profile, or spawn agents.
+
+Revision ownership update: Terra completed the plain-rendering rollback and initial 60/120-minute configuration, plus an initial saved last-arrival field. The core durable cadence remained unfinished after two partial handbacks. Sol `patient_supply` now owns the remaining approved alert scheduler, migration, feed cleanup and focused-test milestone; Terra is idle. This is an escalation for the cross-file scheduling/persistence work. Parent reviewed the partial diff and preserved it. Newly permitted helper: `packages/game-domain/src/alert-cadence.ts` if needed; the batch browser alert scenario may be updated after grouping removal. All other scope and owner-session restrictions remain.
+- Sol completed the durable scheduler and focused regressions. Parent reviewed baseline-relative hunks, including complaint spacing, resolved/reappearing cooldowns, single-item litter, actual offsite return, history-eviction deduplication and same-tick patient wait episodes. Parent requested and worker corrected cadence edge cases before acceptance.
+- Integrated player run: 437/438 passed; remaining assertion expects examination-room upgrade upkeep that a concurrent balance edit changed from 1 to 0. That balance change and the unchanged failing test are outside GS-017. Integrated domain run: 336/337 passed; the remaining forty-encounter surgery-center test exceeded its hardcoded 15-second deadline without an assertion failure. Terra owns a read-only extended-deadline diagnostic. All workspace typechecks and both boundary checks passed.
+- Parent review found legacy ambient deadlines could violate the new 120-minute interval. Sol owns the scoped migration correction and regression before rebuilding the isolated browser artifact. Sol also owns revised isolated production/DEV browser acceptance and cleanup; parent retains final source/evidence review.
+- Concurrent imaging, staff routing, room policy and balance changes are present in shared source paths; preserve them and exclude them from GS-017 ownership. The revision audit is a review artifact, not a staging manifest. Run Vitest from its npm workspace so ignored baseline copies are not discovered.
+- Final review: ambient migration now clamps legacy deadlines once using saved recent history (or a conservative delay when history is missing), then preserves modern deadlines on reload. Parent independently passed all 33 focused alert tests and reviewed the actual migration/test diff. Sol passed post-migration domain/player typechecks and an isolated production build.
